ServiceStatus contains name, current generation ID, next sequence, and ordered generations.
ServiceGeneration contains ID, className, source version digest, historical target ID, state,
inFlight, uncertain, error, preparedAt, promotedAt and retiredAt.
State transitions and target ownership are atomic and contain no external calls.
Reserve generation -> preparing. Attach source digest and target while initializing.
Initialization -> candidate or failed; readiness check -> checking -> ready or failed.
Promote only ready -> active; prior active -> draining.
Reserve a routed call against current active generation before releasing state lock.
Completed calls decrement inFlight; missing replies also increment uncertain.
Drain only when inFlight and uncertain are zero: remove typed target reference and mark retired.
Historical target text does not retain the object; outside direct references still do.
Force retirement is explicit and forbidden for the active generation.
Record forced state only after target acknowledges shutdown; preserve errors on failed force.
